# Project Core

## Language
- All code is English: identifiers, files, folders, tests, commits, branch names.
- User-facing text is Spanish and lives only in `src/ui/strings/es.ts` (English keys). Never hardcode UI text in JSX.

```tsx
// BAD
<button>Nueva partida</button>
// GOOD
<button>{strings.home.newGame}</button>
```

## Typing
- Strict TypeScript. `any` and `unknown` are forbidden.
- External JSON (persistence) is validated with Zod; types are inferred from schemas. Never cast `JSON.parse`.

## Simplicity
- KISS and YAGNI: implement only what the ticket and current plan phase require.
- DRY with judgment: extract on the third repetition or when it is a domain concept. No speculative abstractions.
- Small single-purpose functions. Prefer pure functions and immutable data.

## Comments and logs
- No comments unless they state a non-obvious constraint.
- No `console.*`. Never delete existing comments or logs unless asked.

## Dependencies
- Do not add a dependency without justifying it in the ticket/PR. Prefer the platform and existing deps.

## Commits
- Conventional Commits in English: `feat(engine): add probing`, `fix(ui): lock stroke axis on drag`.

## Done
- Run `pnpm check` (typecheck + lint + tests) before finishing.
